# Make a Lizardfolk monk and photograph the character sheet.
#
# One assertion: with OPT_NATURAL_SPEED set to FLOORED, a creature that can
# hold a weapon never attacks more slowly with an empty limb than the fastest
# weapon it could hold instead. Lizardfolk are the sharpest case, because they
# have real natural attacks -- two claws and a bite -- which lib/races.irh:1634
# rates at 100%, slower than most weapons the same hands can pick up.
#
# The sheet is the oracle. src/Sheet.cpp:151 lists every attack mode with its
# speed, and it draws the Brawl row from KAttr[A_SPD_BRAWL], which is the value
# the floor clamps. src/Term.cpp:597 prints the same number in the traits panel.
#
# Menu letters move when a list changes. Run with a fixed seed; the callers
# tools/check_natural_speed_live.sh supplies one.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
h       # Race:     [h] Lizardfolk
a       # Subrace:  [a] Lizardfolk (Standard)
e       # Class:    [e] Monk
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

# Skill Manager, twice. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available
# without needing to know how many ranks this character has.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

# In the dungeon now. Three keys settle the opening: the room description
# wants dismissing, then two messages want acknowledging. A fourth ESC here
# opens the System Menu instead and every later key lands in it.
ESC ENTER SPACE

# Chargen perks can hand even a monk a real weapon -- this character starts
# with a long sword +3 in the weapon hand. src/Sheet.cpp:162 hides the Brawl
# row whenever SL_WEAPON holds a T_WEAPON, and src/Values.cpp:462 feeds the
# held weapon into the brawl slot anyway, so the hands must be empty before
# the sheet can answer anything about unarmed speed.
i               # Inventory
b s             # Weapon Hand, then Stow: the long sword goes to the pack
@dump:stowed
ESC             # leave the inventory

d               # Display Character Sheet
@dump:sheet1
@quit

